  "reply": "Done.\n\n- **slug.py**: rewrote `slugify` to lowercase, collapse every run of non-alphanumerics into a single `-`, strip leading/trailing `-`, and fall back to `\"item\"` when nothing remains — matching all four SPEC.md points.\n- **tests/test_slug.py**: kept the existing `test_words` and added regression tests for the documented edge cases: mixed separators/punctuation (`\"  Hello,   World!! \"`), collapsed separator runs (`\"---A___B---\"` → `a-b`), and the all-separator case (`\"!!!\"` → `item`).\n\nSPEC.md and acceptance.py were left untouched. The implementation covers the three acceptance asserts, and the test file contains 4 `test_` methods (≥ 3 required).",
